nazuchem-kernel source provenance
===============================

This crate copies ReShiki chemistry modules at
be63a799aa03a83dc6ec74bb294f4d42b89298d3, with explicit host budget injection
and extraction changes described in source headers. An internal copy does
not make the incorporated third-party algorithms original nazuchem code.

Phase A step 3 additionally copies original ReShiki identity orchestration from
crates/model/src/molecule_names.rs at 2df788dc456793c687b934afd6d4b317e3c73ef8,
the private axis-marker codec at 13660ba1bd3fa6cc15bca563607e98550412ffdb,
and the pseudoasymmetric trial classifier from chemistry/stereo_lint.rs at
82b8e6e9c0133fe31a59109ec0adc91507bc8d6f. These helpers use the separately
attributed perception and CIP implementations below; their source headers and
ledger entries record the original ReShiki history and explicit budget changes.

RDKit 2026.03.6, commit 0e0d85f4ca34aeae15dfc0f7cf5503bdb0a8e985:
molecular perception, atomic tables, ring, stereochemistry and CIP algorithms.
